<!--Post: 746--><!--Time: 1092493885-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST746"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->June 29, 1985: Linda Shawn Casey, 31, WSU student, was found dead on the bedroom floor of her home at 356 N. Spruce. She had been bound, beaten, sexually assaulted and stabbed repeatedly. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 746-->
<!--Post: 6524--><!--Time: 1107851452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6524"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sgtrandolph<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sgtrandolph<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 12:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He&#39;s never assaulted his victoms ... and he didn&#39;t in 1986 either ... possible that he may have this time, but the previous murders seemed to have been more about the power over his victims life rather than about sexual relations with them ...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6524-->
<!--Post: 8782--><!--Time: 1109340283-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just read one of the original newspaper articles on this case. Guess what, the water was left running or had been run in the bathroom sink, and there was no drain pipe, so it started leaking to the apartment below. Linda never used the bathroom sink, because of this, so it must have been the killer. She also had a part time job doing &#34;canvassing&#34; which I think is door to door, the company name is &#34;electic shock coalition&#34;.  <BR><a href="http://p216.ezboard.com/fcrimeandjustice13552frm100.showMessage?topicID=386.topic" target=_top>http://p216.ezboard.com/fcrimeandjustice13552frm10 0.showMessage?topicID=386.topic</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8782-->
<!--Post: 9478--><!--Time: 1109537675-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9478"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This was done in an apartment.  Haven&#39;t all the other crimes been done in houses?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9478-->
<!--Post: 10601--><!--Time: 1110052924-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10601"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->V- Didn&#39;t DTDC put in one of his communications something about &#34;running water&#34;? I know that it wasn&#39;t related to this particular possible victim, but hell he has killed so many maybe he got it confused with this one!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10601-->
<!--Post: 10709--><!--Time: 1110145446-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10709"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 1:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No, The Bright family was a apartment.I think the rest of them from BTK-houses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10709-->
<!--Post: 10828--><!--Time: 1110245975-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10828"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 5:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->June 29, 1985	Linda Shawn Casey 	 <BR>356 N Spruce St., age 31.  <BR>She was bound, beaten with a wine bottle on the face and head, sexually assaulted with the bottle, stabbed in the abdomen, vagina, and back, her throat was slashed. 	 <BR>She was found partially clad and dead on the bedroom floor of herapartment.  <BR>No forced entry, no sign of burglary. A knife was found nearby.  <BR>two friends had spoken to her at 4 and 4:30 pm, and at 	5 pm, friends dropped by. At 5:30, tenants in the basement knocked on her door to complain that water from a bathroom sink was dripping into their apartment. <BR>Neither friends nor the neighbors got any answer. Her phone line was cut, and a pair of pants belonging to her boyfriend was missing.	 <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10828-->
<!--Post: 10953--><!--Time: 1110315889-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10953"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 1:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if she was sexually assaulted after she died. Just because it doesn&#39;t fit &#34;exactly&#34; BTK&#39;s pattern, doesn&#39;t mean he didn&#39;t do it.  There are still a lot of similarities.  The Bright case is one that comes to mind as being similar.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10953-->
<!--Post: 11775--><!--Time: 1111156294-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11775"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 6:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->interview with officer on the case: &#40;taken from cj btk forum&#41; <BR> <BR>Brutal murder may be linked  <BR> <BR>It had been six years since anyone heard from BTK when Almon, a homicide detective, was assigned to investigate the brutal murder of Linda Shawn Case. He said he immediately looked at is a possible BTK case, even though BTK seemed to be gone.  <BR>There were some definitely similarities to other BTK cases. The young woman had been bound and tortured before her throat was cut. It appeared to be a random killing. “It was such a gruesome scene,” he said.  <BR>The murder was so high profile that the landlord of the house made money giving tours of the scene. Almon said he quickly put a stop to that by getting a warrant to seal the home.  <BR>Not long after the murder, Almon said he and the other detective, John Blevins, received a tip. An anonymous caller said the Case murder was a BTK case and that there was evidence left in the bathroom.  <BR>Almon said he and Blevins went back to the bathroom and scoured it for evidence. The wallpaper in the room was made to look like old newspaper, so the two men read every word with magnifying glasses.  <BR>Nevertheless, the case was unsolved. A few months later, Almon received a promotion and was transfered out of homicide.  <BR>“It always bothered me as to whether there was really a clue,” he said, “and whether this was a BTK case.”  <BR> <BR>hmmm, a clue in the bathroom....could it have been the missing pipe that the PLUMBER never fixed?  I cant get it out of my head that denny worked with his plumber bro, in one way or more than one way. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11775-->
